WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:01.914
- [Interviewer] All right, so Debbie.

00:00:01.914 --> 00:00:02.747
- Yeah.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.170
- [Interviewer] We met many
years ago and I photographed you

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:10.100
and we just ran into
each other on the street.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:10.933
So, tell me what's new since

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:12.160
the last time I photographed you

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.788
which is about seven,
eight, nine years ago?

00:00:13.788 --> 00:00:14.790
- [Debbie] Well, I'm clean now.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.252
- [Interviewer] You're
clean now which is great.

00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:19.100
- [Debbie] I've been clean.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.340
- [Interviewer] So, the drug
that you were using was what?

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.070
- It was called, crack cocaine.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.970
- [Interviewer] Yes, I've heard of it.

00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:30.165
So, how long have you been clean?

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.340
- Really, I couldn't even tell you.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.660
It's been quite some time.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.440
- [Interviewer] Years?

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.273
- A few years.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.340
- [Interviewer] Is the
temptation still there

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.200
when you see it cause it's everywhere.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.750
- No, but what it does, it bothers me

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.520
to see other people doing it.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.010
If I can get clean, they can too.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.113
It's not a problem.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.830
What I can't stop doing
is smoking cigarettes.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:01.044
Well, I can, but it's harder
to stop those than it is drugs.

00:01:01.044 --> 00:01:03.000
- [Interviewer] What do you think keeps

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.150
all these people on the
street doing crack or heroin?

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.330
- I don't know.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:12.980
Probably, like if they were in a program

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:13.990
like a rehab or whatever,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.340
things that took them out,

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.795
like a family member
dying or stressing, yeah.

00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:20.712
- [Interviewer] Stress.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.297
I don't know, having to
do things that happened

00:01:25.297 --> 00:01:29.020
when they were a kid, being traumatized,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.833
things like that more than likely.

00:01:32.156 --> 00:01:34.778
Or there's some people would just like it.

00:01:34.778 --> 00:01:35.611
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:35.611 --> 00:01:36.444
- Yeah.

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:38.140
- [Interviewer] I almost
think some people are

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.813
driven to self-destruct.

00:01:39.813 --> 00:01:40.646
- Exactly.

00:01:40.646 --> 00:01:42.600
- [Interviewer] And there's
nothing that's going

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.770
to get in the way of that.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.230
- Nothing, they won't let anything.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.460
- [Interviewer] They won't
let anything get in the way

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.500
of them self-destructing.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.333
- Exactly.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.185
- [Interviewer] That's
what I see a lot of.

00:01:50.185 --> 00:01:53.220
- Exactly, exactly, some
of them don't realize

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.164
that's what they're doing.

00:01:55.164 --> 00:01:57.897
They're self-destructing
and they don't realize

00:01:57.897 --> 00:01:58.730
that's exactly what they're doing.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.864
- [Interviewer] No, if you
were explaining it them

00:01:59.864 --> 00:02:01.140
they'd think you're speaking French.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.660
- Yeah, they would, yeah, they'd
think you're the crazy one.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.532
Get away from me.

00:02:05.532 --> 00:02:06.595
- [Interviewer] But, if
you see their behaviors,

00:02:06.595 --> 00:02:09.190
you've lost your kids,
you've lost your family.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.787
- I look at them and I'm like,

00:02:10.787 --> 00:02:12.887
"Oh my God that used to be me."

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.477
And it makes me a little sick to myself.

00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:17.320
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.153
- Yeah.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.760
- [Interviewer] I think
once you've gotten clean

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.740
then you see the picture very clearly.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.740
- Exactly and you see what you
used to be and it's horrible.

00:02:28.068 --> 00:02:28.901
- [Interviewer] When
you're in the middle of it

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:29.734
you don't see anything.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:33.170
- It's horrible, like you just said,

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.070
when you're in the middle of
it you don't see any of that.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.080
You glamorize yourself.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.840
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.000
You look good, you talk good,
you act good, you dress good.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.393
All of that and really it's awful.

00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:56.690
- [Interviewer] Seeing you
before and seeing you now,

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.590
you look healthier, your
energy is much better.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:00.423
- Thank you.

00:03:00.423 --> 00:03:04.120
- [Interviewer] You're more
coherent and clear thinking.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.010
I can just remember all
of this like yesterday

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.840
and you've improved in every--

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.599
I almost didn't recognize you
when I saw you on the street.

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:11.432
- Really?

00:03:11.432 --> 00:03:13.170
- [Interviewer] You just look
so much healthier and better.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.172
- Well thank you.

00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:20.172
I'm trying, I wanted to give
up but that would be giving up

00:03:20.719 --> 00:03:24.093
on myself, be giving up on my family.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.710
Everything, me giving up
on everything and I can't.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.100
- [Interviewer] So, tell
me what got you into drugs

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.767
in the first place, years ago?

00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:40.666
- My family, I hate to say
that, it sounds bad, I know.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:47.555
I was traumatized as a child
from age four until I was 13.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.820
- [Interviewer] By whom?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.970
- A lot of different people.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.440
I'd rather not get into it.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.210
It's pretty bad.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:00.327
Okay, I was molested, I beaten.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.868
I was molested by my brother first.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.370
He was the very first
one at four years old.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:14.083
He penetrated my diaper, he
penetrated me with his thumb.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.310
And that went on for a couple

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.060
of years and he dropped it off.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.720
He didn't die or anything,
but he stopped doing it.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.010
And I had five stepfathers
that took his place.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.713
Separate ones, at different
times periodically.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.010
My mother was a blackout
drunk, a happy drunk,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.690
a violent drunk, whatever
kind of drunk there is,

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.160
she was it.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.490
So, she never knew that
I was being molested

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.560
by my stepfathers.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.910
Every one of them did
it and I had two sisters

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:54.360
but I was the only girl left at home.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.950
So, because I'm the baby girl.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:56.960
- [Interviewer] You're the youngest one.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:57.793
- Yeah.

00:04:59.497 --> 00:05:00.770
- [Interviewer] So, this
went on for quite a while.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.897
- Yeah, until I was 13.

00:05:02.897 --> 00:05:04.790
- [Interviewer] And at 13 what happened?

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:09.790
- I left, I ran away cause
my mother had the audacity

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:15.380
to tell me if anything happened to you,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.610
she knows damn well there did,

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.973
there was also two other men,
I don't even know their names,

00:05:21.975 --> 00:05:23.993
it was back when I was a child.

00:05:32.396 --> 00:05:35.713
If anything happened to
me I wanted it to happen.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.613
I did it, I'm a whore.

00:05:38.613 --> 00:05:39.830
- [Interviewer] According to her.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.797
- According to her I'm a whore.

00:05:41.797 --> 00:05:43.470
"Get out of my house."

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:46.663
And she literally kicked
me out of the house at 13.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.600
Yeah, so I went ahead and left at 13

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.500
and I've been on my own ever since.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.090
- [Interviewer] Where do you go at 13?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:00.713
- All over, traveled, with this.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.030
- [Interviewer] Where'd you grow up?

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.193
- Alabama.

00:06:04.193 --> 00:06:05.390
- [Interviewer] Which city?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:08.100
- Birmingham, in Jefferson County

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:12.470
and I grew up in Shelby County in Chelsea,

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.873
little town called Chelsea.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.080
That's where I went to high school at

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.830
and everything to, it's
called Chelsea High School.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.270
That's why I say high school,

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:25.490
but it's all elementary,
preschool, elementary and all that,

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.870
all in the one.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.703
- [Interviewer] And
when did the drugs come

00:06:27.703 --> 00:06:28.536
into the picture?

00:06:29.843 --> 00:06:31.641
- When I was eight.

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:32.474
- [Interviewer] You were eight?

00:06:32.474 --> 00:06:33.307
- Yeah.

00:06:33.307 --> 00:06:34.920
- [Interviewer] How'd you get
introduced to drugs at eight?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.823
- God rest her soul, my sister, Victoria.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.399
She was the first person to
ever put a pipe in my mouth

00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:45.003
or a needle in my arm when I was 12.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.783
And it released a lot
of the pain out of me.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.740
However, I don't blame her anymore

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.260
because I'm the one they kept doing it.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.193
I did that.

00:07:00.431 --> 00:07:04.090
I'm not mad at her or nothing anymore.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:09.090
However, this man named
Don, he's a counselor,

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:11.240
at the Hilton Treatment Facility,

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.960
which I graduated from.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.653
Also, I'm an alumni from there.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.040
He told me, no, I need to still blame her

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.203
because if it wasn't for her,
I would've never started.

00:07:24.182 --> 00:07:27.755
He doesn't know that,
he doesn't know that.

00:07:27.755 --> 00:07:29.960
I could have did it on my own.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.817
- [Interviewer] I think taking
responsibility is the key.

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:34.990
- But, regardless I kept doing it.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.810
I kept putting the pipe in my mouth.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.765
I kept putting the needle in my arm.

00:07:38.765 --> 00:07:40.730
I did that.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:45.730
She was murdered at 23 and she was shot up

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:49.419
with enough cocaine
poisoning to kill two people

00:07:49.419 --> 00:07:50.869
and that was back in Alabama.

00:07:52.936 --> 00:07:56.463
Luckily I was here but it
still tore me up pretty bad

00:07:56.463 --> 00:07:59.330
because I was really, really close to her.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.533
Really close to her.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.690
My father was murdered when I was three

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.347
and I watched that happen.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.700
He was shot in the back of
the double barrel shotgun.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.100
There was a hole in his
back as big as a baseball,

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.460
as he was breathing,

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.090
you could hear the gravel
going in and out of his back.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.637
I was laying on top of him because

00:08:20.637 --> 00:08:24.523
from the impact of the shot in his back,

00:08:26.122 --> 00:08:27.090
you know the old cars,

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:30.870
they got the little push
button thing on the handle

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.413
and it opens, the old cars.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.510
From the impact of the
shot, it caused his thumb,

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.273
I guess the reflex to open
the door where I was pounding

00:08:42.273 --> 00:08:47.273
on the window, calling him
his name, daddy, daddy, daddy

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.340
and I fell out on top of him.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.710
That's how I know the gravel
going in and out of his back,

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.293
how it sounded.

00:08:54.293 --> 00:08:57.800
- [Interviewer] How much do
you think the environment

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.707
you grew up in played a
part in your addiction?

00:09:00.707 --> 00:09:04.633
- All of it, for me all of it.

00:09:04.633 --> 00:09:06.080
All of it.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.490
Now, that I'm thinking...

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.750
I don't know how to put that.

00:09:18.555 --> 00:09:20.169
I don't know how to put it.

00:09:20.169 --> 00:09:22.308
- [Interviewer] You've
done it and sometimes words

00:09:22.308 --> 00:09:23.808
are not going to--

00:09:24.699 --> 00:09:27.271
- There's nothing I can
say, yeah you're right.

00:09:27.271 --> 00:09:28.873
- [Interviewer] I think you already have.

00:09:28.873 --> 00:09:31.158
The example that you
set is a beautiful one.

00:09:31.158 --> 00:09:32.161
- Thank you.

00:09:32.161 --> 00:09:33.075
- [Interviewer] I'm proud of you.

00:09:33.075 --> 00:09:33.908
- Thank you very much.

00:09:33.908 --> 00:09:35.340
- [Interviewer] You made my
day when I saw you walking out

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.173
towards my car.

00:09:36.173 --> 00:09:37.006
(laughing)
- Thank you.

00:09:37.006 --> 00:09:38.634
- [Interviewer] I know her
but that does look like--

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:39.467
- That doesn't look like her.

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:41.200
- [Interviewer] She should
be worse not better.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.680
- That part, I should be dead.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.997
- [Interviewer] You look better.

00:09:46.361 --> 00:09:51.140
So, the skin condition it
seems like it's improved

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:51.973
since last time.

00:09:51.973 --> 00:09:54.900
- [Debbie] It has, when
he gets hotter though

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.603
and my body temperature
rises, I'll break out more.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.330
It broke out on me at first when I was 14.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:10.250
It's called Neurofibromatosis,
it's not drug related,

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.410
in the ball of nerves at
the bottom of my spine

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.357
there is a disorder in there

00:10:15.357 --> 00:10:17.963
and the doctors were unable to locate it.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:23.624
When I was younger I also
went to a dermatologist

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:27.310
and he said it was a
deficiency of vitamin A.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:31.653
I was fed all sorts of
vitamin A, it didn't work.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.460
Like I said, a few minutes
ago, it's not drug related.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:44.460
It is a nerve disorder
in my ball of nerves

00:10:44.612 --> 00:10:46.224
at the bottom of my spine.

00:10:46.224 --> 00:10:47.447
- [Interviewer] And it's caused by stress

00:10:47.447 --> 00:10:48.280
or something like that?

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:52.010
- [Debbie] Yes, it's caused
from being traumatized.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:56.100
Like I was from age four, even until now

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.260
but I am doing so much better.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.083
- [Interviewer] Yeah, it
looks much better yet.

00:11:02.083 --> 00:11:05.420
- [Debbie] This is looking
better, I'm looking better,

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:09.420
I'm feeling better, I am better.

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:10.400
- [Interviewer] Yes, you are.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.103
So, how many years were you using?

00:11:15.175 --> 00:11:16.758
- I'm 50 years old,

00:11:17.736 --> 00:11:20.236
I know I look 90 but whatever,

00:11:22.001 --> 00:11:25.168
and I used for 42 of those years, man.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.830
If I can do it, anybody can do it.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.297
Anybody, I don't care who you are

00:11:32.297 --> 00:11:35.954
or what you're doing, you can stop it.

00:11:35.954 --> 00:11:37.793
You know, you can stop it.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:39.483
Look at me.

